Error [E0121]: `values` was consumed by a lambda that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> move_lambda_index_and_slice_captures_stop_at_the_rust_prefix.jet:6:11
    |
  6 |     print(values.len())
    |           ^^^^^^
  --> move_lambda_index_and_slice_captures_stop_at_the_rust_prefix.jet:5:30
    |
  5 |     call(() -> { print(values[0]) })
    |                              ^^^ `values` moved to a lambda that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `values` after the move, or give a lambda that captures it a copy with `~values` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
